        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Nicopolis</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">25 September 1396</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Before the fortress of Nicopolis on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">A crusader army under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor">Sigismund</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, with a French contingent nominally led by John, Count of Nevers, against an Ottoman force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Sultan Bayezid I</a>. Numbers are heavily contested: 19th-century German historians reached about 7,500 to 15,000 Christians and about 12,000 to 20,000 Turks, while chroniclers give far higher figures.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The crusaders were routed. Many were killed or captured, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor">Sigismund</a> escaped by boat, and the siege of Nicopolis was lifted.</span></div>
        </div>
